.TH df "" "Command"
.SH NAME
df \- print free space on file systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdf [\-a] [\-i] [\-t] [\fIdirectory ...\fB] [\fIfilesystem ...\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
df -- print free space on file systems
Usage:	df [ -a ][ -i ][ -t ] filesystem ...
Options:
	-a	Give entries only for mounted devices
	-i	Summarize i-node usage
	-t	Give total number of blocks on device
.HE
.B df
prints the amount of free space on one or more file systems.
Each named argument may be a block- or character-special file
(the raw or block file system device), or an ordinary directory, in
which case
.B df
looks up the device that directory resides on by searching
.B /dev
for a special file with a matching device number.
.PP
With no arguments,
.B df
reports on the file system that holds the current directory (unless
.B \-a
is given alone, in which case it reports only on the mounted file
systems, as below).
With one or more arguments, it reports on each in turn.
.PP
For each file system,
.B df
prints its name, then the number of free blocks over the total number
of blocks (excluding the space used by the i-list), and that fraction
again as a percentage.
.IP \fB\-a\fR 0.4i
Also report on every file system currently listed in
.B /etc/mnttab
(or, if that does not exist, in the older
.B /etc/mtab
format), in addition to any
.I directory
or
.I filesystem
arguments given.
.IP \fB\-i\fR
Also print the number of free i-nodes over the total number of
i-nodes, and that fraction as a percentage.
.IP \fB\-t\fR
Also print the total number of blocks on the device.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 1.4i
\fB/etc/mnttab\fR	table of mounted file systems
\fB/etc/mtab\fR	older-format mount table, used if /etc/mnttab is absent
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR du ,
.BR mkfs ,
.B mount
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B df
complains and skips a file system it cannot stat, cannot open, cannot
read a superblock from, or whose superblock does not pass its
consistency check; it exits with status 1 if any file system was
skipped for such a reason, or if given an unrecognized option.
